"""Compact-note design and measured results, generated from audited call records."""
import json
from pathlib import Path
from html import escape as e
from site_navigation import project_tabs,experiment_subtabs
from build_answering_results import CSS,details,table as raw_table,text,link
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1];P=ROOT/'research/notes-optimization'
NAMES={'reactive':'Reactive','legacy_all':'Old notes · all snapshots','legacy_latest':'Old notes · latest snapshot','legacy':'Old notes · all snapshots','snapshot':'Compact replacement','delta':'Incremental edits'}
def fmt(x):return 'Unexposed' if x is None else f'{x:,.0f}'
def main():
 number=0
 def table(ignored,*args,**kwargs):
  nonlocal number
  number+=1
  return raw_table(number,*args,**kwargs)
 d=json.loads((P/'results.json').read_text());prompts=json.loads((P/'prompts.json').read_text());p=d['protocol'];body='<header class="hero"><p class="small">4 November 2026 · Structured-note optimization</p><h1>Compact notes that track meeting changes</h1></header><section id="findings"><h2>Current findings and work</h2><ul>'
 bullets=[('The old approach repeats full snapshots; this study tests one replacement state and small edits.','#design'),('Both candidate prompts preserve ownership, quantities, uncertainty and evidence for genuine revisions.','#prompts'),('Six development questions guide prompt selection; twelve questions from six other meetings test the frozen design.','#protocol'),('Accuracy, request-time thinking and the entire earlier token cost determine the comparison.','#results')]
 body+=''.join('<li>'+e(t)+' '+link(u,'Details')+'</li>' for t,u in bullets)+'</ul><p class="small">A completed inference run is reviewed against source evidence before an accuracy claim is added. '+link('../todo.html','Project TODO')+' · '+link('../daily-log.html','Daily log')+' · '+link('answering-results.html#s2-tradeoff','Earlier structured-note results')+'</p></section>'
 body+='<section id="design"><h2>1. What changes in the note process?</h2><p>The note writer receives the new 25–40 s transcript chunk, up to ten seconds of earlier speech for reference resolution, and one current note state. It never receives a future question. At question time, the reader retains the full available transcript and receives one current state.</p>'
 body+=table(1,'Note policies and the information passed between calls.', ['Policy','Writer input','Writer output','Question-time notes'],[
 ['Old · all snapshots','Full transcript prefix + all valid earlier snapshots.','Another full snapshot, up to twelve notes.','All valid snapshots.'],['Old · latest snapshot','The same saved old writer calls.','No new writer calls in this control.','Only the final eligible old snapshot.'],['Compact replacement','New chunk + recent reference speech + one earlier state.','One replacement state: up to sixteen facts and eight changes.','One current state.'],['Incremental edits','New chunk + recent reference speech + one earlier state.','Up to six add/update/retire edits; an empty list means no change.','One current state with up to sixteen facts and eight recent changes.']])
 body+='<p>For incremental edits, the program assigns stable note IDs, checks source availability and rejects exact duplicate facts. When an edit marks a genuine revision, it saves the previous fact and source along with the new state. The full version archive remains on disk; the model receives the latest eight changes. Retired notes remain in the audit archive. A 4,096-token state limit guards memory growth; rejected updates and any capacity failures count in the audit.</p><p><strong>Illustrative example:</strong> “A will send the invitation Friday” followed by “I will send it tomorrow instead” should update the same task and preserve the Friday → tomorrow change. A different task with a Friday deadline should keep a separate note. “I uploaded it” remains a speaker’s report until later speech verifies access.</p></section>'
 body+='<section id="protocol"><h2>2. Experiment and evaluation</h2><ul><li>Reuse both pinned Qwen3-30B readers, the original response prompt and the original request-time output limits.</li><li>Compare reactive, old-all, old-latest, compact replacement and incremental-edit conditions on the same six development questions.</li><li>Use one greedy Instruct run and two Thinking request seeds; earlier note generation uses seed 23.</li><li>Choose the policy using source-complete answers, unsupported claims, duplication, event changes and cost, then freeze it before the additional-meeting test.</li><li>Review final answers against source-based required facts; source-ID validity and JSON format are checked separately.</li></ul>'
 body+='<p>Thinking tokens are the model’s native reasoning tokens after the user request. Earlier thinking tokens are counted separately. Instruct exposes ordinary output tokens but no separate native thinking channel. Total generated tokens include earlier reasoning, note text, request-time reasoning, answer text and delimiters; they measure output volume rather than FLOPs. Each meeting’s writer calls count once per condition. The old-latest control retains the full old writer cost.</p><p>The additional test uses twelve questions in '+e(', '.join(d['additional_selection']['meetings']))+'. These meetings were selected by split and timing metadata before development outputs were inspected; they are held out from this prompt-selection step. Later automatic-transcript checks reuse the existing anonymous speaker labels to avoid introducing changing annotation aliases.</p></section>'
 body+='<section id="results"><h2>3. Actual outputs and token costs</h2>'
 if not d['summaries']:body+='<p>GPU experiments are running or queued; answer accuracy has not yet been measured for the new policies.</p>'
 else:
  rows=[]
  for r in d['summaries']:
   accuracy=(str(r['complete'])+'/'+str(r['questions'])) if r['reviewed']==r['questions'] else 'Review pending ('+str(r['reviewed'])+'/'+str(r['questions'])+')'
   rows.append([e(r['stage']),e(r['model'])+' · seed '+str(r['seed']),NAMES.get(r['policy'],r['policy']),accuracy,fmt(r['mean_request_thinking_tokens']),fmt(r['mean_request_input_tokens']),fmt(r['earlier_generated_tokens']),fmt(r['total_generated_tokens'])])
  body+=table(2,'Answer completeness and generated-token cost per question set and request seed; earlier work is shared across request-seed repetitions.', ['Set','Reader','Notes','Complete','Mean request thinking','Mean request input','Earlier generated','Total generated'],rows)
 if d['states']:
  rows=[[e(r['model']),NAMES.get(r['policy'],r['policy']),str(r['calls']),str(r['invalid_calls']),fmt(r['maximum_state_tokens']),e(json.dumps(r['rejected_edits']))] for r in d['states']]
  body+=table(3,'Note-state validation; a valid edit is still subject to semantic review.', ['Writer','Policy','Calls','Invalid calls','Largest state, tokens','Rejected edits'],rows)
 body+='</section><section id="examples"><h2>4. Inspect actual answers and notes</h2>'
 for a in d['answers']:
  title=a['model']+' · '+NAMES.get(a['policy'],a['policy'])+' · seed '+str(a['seed'])+' · '+a['question'];content='<p><strong>Reference:</strong> '+e(a['reference_answer'])+'</p>'+text(a['answer'] or '[No complete final answer]')+'<p class="small">Request thinking: '+fmt(a['request_thinking_tokens'])+' tokens; input: '+fmt(a['request_input_tokens'])+' tokens.</p>'
  content+=details('Original source evidence','<ul>'+''.join('<li>'+e(x['id'])+' · '+e(x['speaker'])+': '+e(x['text'])+'</li>' for x in a['source_evidence'])+'</ul>')
  if a['review']:content+='<p>'+e(a['review']['reason'])+'</p>'
  body+=details(title,content)
 for r in d['states']:
  content=''.join(details(s['meeting']+' · '+f"{s['source_cutoff']:.1f} s",'<pre>'+e(json.dumps(s['state'],ensure_ascii=False,indent=2))+'</pre>') for s in r['final_states']);body+=details(r['model']+' · '+NAMES.get(r['policy'],r['policy'])+' · final meeting states',content)
 body+='</section><section id="literature"><h2>5. Literature behind the design</h2><p>The papers motivate explicit memory updates, self-contained facts and temporal links. Most compare retrieval-based or trained memories with other inputs; the present study tests prompt-only notes while retaining the transcript.</p>'
 rows=[[link(x['source'],x['title']),e(x['venue']),e(x['method']),e(x['relevance'])] for x in d['literature']['papers']];body+=table(4,'Verified primary sources and the design choices they motivate.', ['Paper','Publication','Method','Adaptation for this study'],rows)+details('Literature gaps and full digest','<ul>'+''.join('<li>'+e(x['statement'])+'</li>' for x in d['literature']['gaps'])+'</ul><p>'+link('../research/notes-optimization/LITERATURE.md','Read the focused review')+'</p>')+'</section>'
 body+='<section id="prompts"><h2>Appendix: exact prompts and resources</h2>'+details('Compact replacement prompt','<pre>'+e(prompts['snapshot'])+'</pre>')+details('Incremental edit prompt','<pre>'+e(prompts['delta'])+'</pre>')
 body+=details('GPU allocation and run status','<p>Each job requests one H100 80 GB. Text weights and an 8 GiB KV cache share GPU 0; writer and reader execute sequentially through vLLM with CUDA graphs and prefix caching. No S1, TTS or ASR services share the GPU. The two development jobs are independent; later experiments depend on reviewed development results. Maximum two experiment GPUs active.</p>'+table(5,'Saved execution snapshot; this page updates when evidence is collected.', ['Reader','Set','State','Calls','Answers'],[[e(r['model']),e(r['stage']),e(r['status']),str(r['calls']),str(r['answers'])] for r in d['resources']]))+'<p>'+link('../research/notes-optimization/results.json','Results and selected states')+' · '+link('../research/notes-optimization/prompts.json','Prompts and output schemas')+'</p></section>'
 body+='<section id="next"><h2>Next steps and goals</h2><ul><li>Review development outputs to select an efficient policy that preserves answer quality and event changes.</li><li>Test the frozen policy on additional meetings to check whether the development result transfers.</li><li>Test automatic transcripts and a cheaper Instruct writer with a Thinking reader to separate perception, note quality and reasoning cost.</li></ul></section>'
 js="function reveal(){const t=document.getElementById(decodeURIComponent(location.hash.slice(1)));if(!t)return;for(let p=t;p;p=p.parentElement)if(p.tagName==='DETAILS')p.open=true;requestAnimationFrame(()=>t.scrollIntoView());}addEventListener('load',reveal);addEventListener('hashchange',reveal);"
 page='<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark"><meta name="description" content="Compact structured-note experiments for token efficiency and tracking meeting changes."><title>Structured-note optimization · AI2AI Duplex</title><link rel="stylesheet" href="../assets/site.css"><style>'+CSS+'</style></head><body><a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a><header class="site-nav"><div class="nav-inner"><a class="brand" href="../index.html">AI2AI Duplex</a>'+project_tabs('experiments','../')+'</div></header><div class="container collection-nav">'+experiment_subtabs('notes')+'</div><main id="main" class="container results">'+body+'</main><script>'+js+'</script></body></html>\n';(ROOT/'experiments/structured-notes.html').write_text(page)
if __name__=='__main__':main()
